Z||000000||80's BOY||05-23-2001||09:43 AM||||my friend needs help with his 4cyl SE (just purchased) the oxygen sensor is disconnected, and we can't find the wire. it bogs down real bad on takeoff, then raps out like a powerband on a motorcycle. probably out of time, but i've never seen a 4cyl fiero before so i can't help much. any ideas would help.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||05-23-2001||10:38 AM||||It probably bogs out off the line when it is warm because it's running in open loop because the O2 sensor is not connected. Everything the computer does depends on that O2 sensor so he needs to get it connected.<P>He should also solder the connector on and use shrink wrap because the O2 sensor only produces a max voltage of 1 volt. Any unnecessary resistance will cause inaccurate readings and the car won’t run right. Don’t use crimp connectors.   <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||05-23-2001||10:46 AM||||Just to aid in your search for the wire, the wire comes out of a harness from the left rear side of the engine compartment.  I think the harness might actually be attached very close by, and then the wire with a black connector pops out of the plastic loom tubing.  This is just from memory, I will try to remember to check to make sure tonight and I'll get a pic if I can.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||05-23-2001||01:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 80's BOY:<BR><B>my friend needs help with his 4cyl SE (just purchased) the oxygen sensor is disconnected, and we can't find the wire. it bogs down real bad on takeoff, then raps out like a powerband on a motorcycle. probably out of time, but i've never seen a 4cyl fiero before so i can't help much. any ideas would help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bogging on a 4-cyl is also cause by.....<P>a 4-cyl engine!  Put in a 6 and the problem will go away....<P>Sorry guys and gals' couldn't resist.<P>||||reg||6
